{"title":"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2018 AMC 10A #25</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">2018 AMC 12A #25</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(PaperMath&#39;s_sum)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (PaperMath's sum)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(#21-#25)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (#21-#25)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and nonzero digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit integer each of whose digits is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />; let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be2b1de79fff66db67de3b18303bdd2912b7ae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit integer each of whose digits is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e173907ca992482385a50c6f62ede920362b1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />-digit (not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit) integer each of whose digits is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. What is the greatest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> for which there are at least two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee2898536ac76874d818128c0569ec0144a18356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_n - B_n = A_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bbdd14d411a771654ba58aa06462df94668ae4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 14 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 16 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 18 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By geometric series, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/48689197268e4c20da5a0203f91da0fe6484543f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{8} A_n&amp;=a\\bigl(\\phantom{ }\\underbrace{111\\cdots1}_{n\\text{ digits}}\\phantom{ }\\bigr)&amp;&amp;=a\\left(1+10+10^2+\\cdots+10^{n-1}\\right)&amp;&amp;=a\\cdot\\frac{10^n-1}{9}, \\\\ B_n&amp;=b\\bigl(\\phantom{ }\\underbrace{111\\cdots1}_{n\\text{ digits}}\\phantom{ }\\bigr)&amp;&amp;=b\\left(1+10+10^2+\\cdots+10^{n-1}\\right)&amp;&amp;=b\\cdot\\frac{10^n-1}{9}, \\\\ C_n&amp;=c\\bigl(\\phantom{ }\\underbrace{111\\cdots1}_{2n\\text{ digits}}\\phantom{ }\\bigr)&amp;&amp;=c\\left(1+10+10^2+\\cdots+10^{2n-1}\\right)&amp;&amp;=c\\cdot\\frac{10^{2n}-1}{9}. \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"525\" height=\"166\" />\nBy substitution, we rewrite the given equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee2898536ac76874d818128c0569ec0144a18356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_n - B_n = A_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" /> as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5590f96592936c5848fb3b609d6cd140f84d7419.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c\\cdot\\frac{10^{2n}-1}{9} - b\\cdot\\frac{10^n-1}{9} = a^2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{10^n-1}{9}\\right)^2.\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"46\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/a/8ca2e35b75c4df064d304af92e6924a932fe9325.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5fa10f1dc316d35520fc7f54f3030f30732f76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n &gt; 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" /> We divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541de476733ad1d8ab860b44f88edb6ad9d45b38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10^n-1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" /> and then rearrange:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f49e8355ef830d1af99a8da8f12ab37920f77e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} c\\left(10^n+1\\right) - b &amp;= a^2\\cdot\\frac{10^n-1}{9} \\\\ 9c\\left(10^n+1\\right) - 9b &amp;= a^2\\left(10^n-1\\right) \\\\ \\left(9c-a^2\\right)10^n &amp;= 9b-9c-a^2. &amp;&amp;(\\bigstar) \\end{align*}\" width=\"350\" height=\"92\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b89e4306280310ed9e642c605fdcf4307c03276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=10^n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875816dba06e32edf79fcfbb793af13f73bdca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> is a linear equation with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1d002db36c51a77f8fbc6314e96756fc793e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a one-to-one function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875816dba06e32edf79fcfbb793af13f73bdca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> has at least two solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> it has at least two solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e228943301b048f242377b3b24717037d5996f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> We conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875816dba06e32edf79fcfbb793af13f73bdca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> must be an identity, so we get the following system of equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1ddcdb7c571109b962b41bbcaf200455880cc3e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 9c-a^2&amp;=0, \\\\ 9b-9c-a^2&amp;=0. \\end{align*}\" width=\"132\" height=\"43\" />\nThe first equation implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5635c86df7084ea99a418b503bada70ccab31b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\frac{a^2}{9}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"41\" /> Substituting this into the second equation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/8/ae8bf2b3859e7fd1d9ea5a1fed898f784c019b11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{2a^2}{9}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"41\" /> \n</p><p>To maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b52b468ccf341ce91cc0172aae859ec68186462f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = a + \\frac{a^2}{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"41\" /> we need to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef9cdc7c7d46920eac603663914e0d9261a99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93032f1ab8b685d84a767a2fde0d9006a464b5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> The possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a36920b87022605be19fb63bed0f9f485bbdb313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9,18,9),(6,8,4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926f7978cb2b088982f718d301677f64005397b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,2,1),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/6/af640e6791cbd98c3c00e3a4dfb64ef6b0666177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9,18,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> is invalid. Therefore, the greatest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8112fc504fd86270cafc00cd29713d4a16edb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+8+4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 18}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"168\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~CantonMathGuy (Solution)\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (Revision)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Immediately start trying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. These give the system of equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/52123d34c110b0f7ea63f0aa9c0c68e19a3884ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11c - b = a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b907c3179b2bf6a7e2fb999647c02962fe14f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1111c - 11b = (11a)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"19\" /> (which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282dfce2a740538724961229b6ce5d4959893d81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101c - b = 11a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"123\" height=\"15\" />). These imply that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/69931d7ef7773bc33ae40c6a17fd3b19782da76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 = 9c$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, so the possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eba74536ce5f55f37ed7c4b99092e3ad6c1a3cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> pairs are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef3d449e9687f53a8b9a8fff1f978320cd480b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9, 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a6aa4fae2c4e4c29b43f57a15cd214e525e111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d261236ea904095d8d185a456444545b5206013b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The first puts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> out of range but the second makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b447277e683dbf98cb0cbcbddf0debfd717e1c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 8$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. We now know the answer is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac8e8251f822d658f235ca831b341d4c6b4269b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 8 + 4 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We now only need to know whether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/8227c43fe6f2415688e4793e82a3185ef8c6e74c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" /> might work for any larger <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We will always get equations like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba25e387282bd4a14026aef766dc436a994708b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100001c - b = 11111a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"177\" height=\"15\" /> where the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> coefficient is very close to being nine times the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> coefficient. Since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> term will be quite insignificant, we know that once again <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9698c992334be77221be8c8c819909eca34fde9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06df0ca2db6ae1e5ff10e67ef40fe28c79691943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9c$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b27a227147ad2961f3d48211b818e37b30ff223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 9, c = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> is our only hope to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Substituting and dividing through by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we will have something like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a1aa812bd164ee790446a69d5287b8fde39d4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100001 - \\frac{b}{9} = 99999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" />. No matter what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> really was, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is out of range (and certainly isn't <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as we would have needed).\n</p><p>The answer then is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/98679df9a9626db768969306810168a3e819be96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The given equation can be written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edcc0f97cca7fe54ae663e0fcb5c13e36b96a465.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c \\cdot (\\phantom{ } \\overbrace{1111 \\ldots 1111}^{2n\\text{ digits}}\\phantom{ }) - b \\cdot (\\phantom{ } \\overbrace{11 \\ldots 11}^{n\\text{ digits}} \\phantom{ }) = a^2 \\cdot (\\phantom{ } \\overbrace{11 \\ldots 11}^{n\\text{ digits}} \\phantom{ })^2.\\]\" width=\"417\" height=\"40\" />\nDivide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b2dd9cecfde966c9094b2cea555fc13a65ea84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overbrace{11 \\ldots 11}^{n\\text{ digits}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"39\" /> on both sides:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7da1baba668bcdff82bf10c06d6177f39e5fb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c \\cdot (\\phantom{ } \\overbrace{1000 \\ldots 0001}^{n+1\\text{ digits}}\\phantom{ }) - b = a^2 \\cdot (\\phantom{ } \\overbrace{11 \\ldots 11}^{n\\text{ digits}} \\phantom{ }).\\]\" width=\"312\" height=\"40\" />\nNext, split the first term to make it easier to deal with:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a3d86440a42205406b72e26b10da27dc385ea0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2c + c \\cdot (\\phantom{ }\\overbrace{99 \\ldots 99}^{n\\text{ digits}}\\phantom{ }) - b &amp;= a^2 \\cdot (\\phantom{ } \\overbrace{11 \\ldots 11}^{n\\text{ digits}} \\phantom{ }) \\\\ 2c - b &amp;= (a^2 - 9c) \\cdot (\\phantom{ }\\overbrace{11 \\ldots 11}^{n\\text{ digits}}\\phantom{ }). \\end{align*}\" width=\"368\" height=\"90\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98e403ef62c6a5fa459cbb3afc71d48449e3d797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c - b$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e325cddc7848b8ddd23cfb411cabd22f548a167.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 - 9c$\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> are constants and because there must be at least two distinct values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/08138509e0c3195e1eaa7c9d2c59bb683377846d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c - b = a^2 - 9c = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" /> Thus, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc3f96adc64ed251a59a9cf2baef771f6a4a3dcb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2c&amp;=b, \\\\ a^2&amp;=9c. \\end{align*}\" width=\"61\" height=\"40\" />\nKnowing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are single digit positive integers and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06df0ca2db6ae1e5ff10e67ef40fe28c79691943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9c$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> must be a perfect square, the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> that satisfy both equations are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63ced9520da3dc23518681b79b9c32c35253ab7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,2,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26bb4d4237f0aae98df140f345c854ee4da0c4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,8,4).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be58ff4f8b7892f191d66b5cd660c3c85908034c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 8 + 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 18}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"168\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~LegionOfAvatars (Solution)\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (Reformatting)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28PaperMath.27s_sum.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(PaperMath's_sum)\">Solution 4 (PaperMath's sum)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (PaperMath&#39;s sum)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=PaperMath%E2%80%99s_sum\" title=\"PaperMath’s sum\">PaperMath’s sum</a>, the answer is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8112fc504fd86270cafc00cd29713d4a16edb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+8+4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 18}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"168\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_.28Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(Easy)\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy (Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DgtlLI9GaWY?si=WgXKpx2PCF1cftuE\">https://youtu.be/DgtlLI9GaWY?si=WgXKpx2PCF1cftuE</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.2321-.2325.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(#21-#25)\">Video Solution (#21-#25)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (#21-#25)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLpxy89D2tvVow8EoCSsNY3Y-2SwJly_SZ&amp;si=aEJ3Ttjck10aCIUH\">https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLpxy89D2tvVow8EoCSsNY3Y-2SwJly_SZ&amp;si=aEJ3Ttjck10aCIUH</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2018amc10a/470\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2018amc10a/470</a>\n</p><p>~ dolphin7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A\">2018 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2018 AMC